{{Politics of Balisca}}

The '''Secretariat of Education and Integration''' ('''SECEI''') is the [[Secretariat Council (Balisca)|secretariat]] of the [[Government and politics of Balisca|Government of Balisca]] responsible for proposing and carrying out the government policy on [[Education in Balisca|education]] and [[W:Vocational education|vocational training]], including all the teachings of the [[Baliscan education system|education system]] except [[List of universities in Balisca|university]] education. Likewise, it is also the responsibility of this Department the promotion of cooperative actions and, in coordination with the [[Secretariat of Culture and Social Inclusion (Balisca)|Secretariat of Culture and Social Inclusion]], the [[W:Integration of immigrants|integration of immigrants]] (job placement, [[W:Language immersion|language immersion]], [[W:anti-bias curriculum|anti-bias curriculum]], etc).

The [[Education in Balisca]] is established as a decentralized system in which the [[Cantons of Balisca|cantons]] have powers over the [[W:Basic education|basic]] and [[W:Secondary education|secondary education]] while the central government establishes the general basis of the system and it is responsible for the [[W:Tertiary education|tertiary education]]. Since the adoption of the [[Iniziatiba Basica Academic Confederal|Confederal Academic Baseline Initiative]] (IBAC) in 1922, the [[Cantons of Balisca|cantons]] authorized the establishment of confederal-level councils to compile statistics nationwide and make recommendations for baseline standards and requirements that each region would meet. Cantons that fail to meet the standards for a consecutive two schooling periods will have their programs abrogated by their region.

The Secretary is assisted by the [[Secretary of State for Education (Spain)|Secretary of State for Education]], the Secretary-General for Vocational Training (with the rank of Under-Secretary) and the Under-Secretary of Integration. In addition, in order to coordinate the education system it exists the Sectoral Conference on Education that is composed by the Education Secretary and the Regional Councils of Education. 

